## 5. Data flow

```
S-PROBE artifact ──I1(read-only, hashed)──▶ Decision Brief ──▶ ║FOUNDER║ ──▶ Decision Record
                                                                              │
                                             ┌────────────────────────────────┤
                                             ▼                                ▼
                                   I5 Evidence(external)              I3 gate verifier
                                             │                                │
                                             ▼                                ▼
                                   C8 lattice: verified            I4 release | abandon
                                       → integrated (K8)                      │
                                                                     ┌────────┴────────┐
                                                                     ▼                 ▼
                                                              wave-2 nodes        C9 §7 falsifier
```

Flow invariants:

- **One-way.** Nothing downstream of C3 writes back to C1. The probe is evidence, not a
  work product to be reconciled with the verdict.
- **One writer per artifact** (K8/Ω10-discipline): Runtime writes the brief; the founder
  writes `decision:`; the resolver writes only DAG state. No component writes another's
  artifact.
- **Single human cut.** Exactly one edge crosses the A4 boundary in each direction (evidence
  in, resolution out). Adding a second would multiply founder-channel demand against a
  constant-capacity channel (Ω-22).
- **Cost.** One `decisions` budget unit. Zero `exec_seconds`. Non-fungible with every other
  dimension (K4 §10, Ω-09) — no amount of compute substitutes for it.

